   "branch": "capital-system",
   "adv": false,
   "html": "<h2>What it is</h2>\n<p>The <strong>capital system</strong> is every way wealth can be stored, moved and grown: money, debts, ownership stakes, physical things, digital tokens, and the skills and relationships inside you. This map lays them out as one connected tree.</p>\n<h2>How the map is organised</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The tree is organised by what things are.</strong> Each branch is a kind of asset or a body of ideas. A page lives in one place on the tree and links to everything else it touches.</li>\n<li><strong>One question sorts money and claims:</strong> <em>whose liability is it, and what is it a claim on?</em> See <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/claims-and-liabilities\" data-page=\"claims-and-liabilities\">Claims and Liabilities</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>One model sorts stores of wealth by risk:</strong> the <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/cartography-of-wealth\" data-page=\"cartography-of-wealth\">Cartography of Wealth</a>, which maps each store by how embodied in you it is and how visible it is to the state, and names the one thing most likely to kill it.</li>\n<li><strong>How things trade right now</strong> (for example, crypto moving like high-growth tech shares) is a separate question. It changes with conditions, so it lives under <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/market-regimes\" data-page=\"market-regimes\">Market Regimes</a> rather than shaping the tree.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>The branches</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/foundation\" data-page=\"foundation\">Foundation</a> — the ideas everything rests on.</li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/money\" data-page=\"money\">Money &amp; Liquidity</a> — what money is, and its hierarchy from gold to bank deposits.</li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/personal-capital\" data-page=\"personal-capital\">Human &amp; Social Capital</a> — skills, health, reputation and network.</li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/fixed-income\" data-page=\"fixed-income\">Fixed Income</a>, <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/equities\" data-page=\"equities\">Equities</a>, <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/real-assets\" data-page=\"real-assets\">Real Assets</a>, <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/digital-assets\" data-page=\"digital-assets\">Digital Assets</a>, <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/derivatives\" data-page=\"derivatives\">Derivatives</a> — the asset classes.</li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/portfolio\" data-page=\"portfolio\">Portfolio &amp; Risk</a> — combining them so that no single failure clears the board.</li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/markets\" data-page=\"markets\">Markets &amp; Plumbing</a>, <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/measure\" data-page=\"measure\">Measure</a>, <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/practice\" data-page=\"practice\">In Practice</a>, <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/tools\" data-page=\"tools\">Tools</a> — the plumbing, the scorecard and the practicalities.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Key rule:</strong> this is a reference, not advice. It explains how things work so you can judge for yourself.</p>\n</blockquote>",
